    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38840" root="ملأَ" body-key="m">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلْآنٌ</span></b>  (S, K) [and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلْآنُ</span>, as it forms in the]
fem. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلْآنَةٌ</span> (K) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلْأَى</span>; (S;) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِلَآءٌ</span>; (K;)
<i>Full:</i> (S, K) said of a vessel, &amp;c. (S, TA.)
The masc. is also written and pronounced <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلَان</span>;
and the fem., <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلَا</span>: (TA:) and the vulgar say
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِنَاءٌ مَلَا</span> <i>A full vessel.</i> (S, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلْآنٌ من الكَرَمِ</span>
(tropical:)  [<i>Full of generosity</i>]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَمْلُوْءٌ</span>.

